      "description": "The user is projected onto the visual entity of the snake's mouth, as the textual material explicitly maps it to a vagina, creating an implicit identification or focus on this body part. The user is not directly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the projection occurs through the act of perceiving the visual material and interpreting it via the provided textual analogy, which directs attention and potentially identification onto the snake's mouth as the central object of comparison.",
